% The prompt is a diagnostic and goes to stderr with the rest of what the
% REPL says about itself, so that a session whose rows are redirected to a
% file gets rows and nothing else.  The wrapper decides whether to print one
% from whether stdin is a terminal; this case sets AWKLOG_PROMPT directly,
% since a harness has no terminal to offer.
%
% The session ends at end of input rather than with .quit, so it also pins the
% newline that closes the line the last prompt started -- the user pressed
% Ctrl-D on it, and without it the shell's own prompt would land on it.
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
